`LogNorm()` is a generated norm class built on `Normalize`. Its `autoscale()` first clears both limits, then calls `autoscale_None(A)`. For the log-based norm, `autoscale_None` overrides the base method by filtering `A` down to values whose log transform is finite, then delegates to `Normalize.autoscale_None`, which sets `self.vmin = A.min()` and `self.vmax = A.max()` when both are unset. The test array contains only positive finite values, so the filtered array is the same data, whose minimum is `0.001` and maximum is `8.0`.

## Answer
{"vmax":8.0,"vmin":0.001}
